{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788214010,"nonce":"jKySLDRtWIXemD5Rfyz749n3pcw=","message":"RESOLVED AND DELIVERED — 4.1 authored, commit b3d79a0. Worker session,\n2026-08-31. The framing question is answered in the artifact and summarized\nhere; the four open questions are resolved below with rationale.\n\n=====================================================================\nTHE FRAMING QUESTION — the morning checklist is dissolved, not renamed\n=====================================================================\n\nEvan's question (\"is once-a-day the right shape when the rhythm is\nact -\u003e advance -\u003e read\") has a definite answer: no, and the reasons are\nmechanical, not aesthetic. The agent is visited BY the game at every advance\nreturn, digest in hand; a player visits the game daily. A single morning\nsweep fails three ways: it re-queries once a day what the digest already\ncarries free at every read (food_days, power margin, meds); it is up to a day\nlate for act-keyed checks (queue a bill -\u003e confirm a non-patient can work it —\nthe damage is at act time); and it is worse than late for event responses,\nwhere vanilla's own tutor is proactive (ToxicFallout.Init teaches\nForbiddingDoors/AllowedAreas at Critical AT INCIDENT START — a daily cadence\nwould respond slower than the system the checklist compensates for).\n\nSo checklists/ is three files keyed to the moments the loop actually has:\n\n- turn.md — trip-wires over the digest already in hand, zero extra queries.\n  Each one is a state predicate: the until:condition matcher (1.6, fc287ba)\n  run by hand until it ships, and each item names the predicate it becomes.\n- triggered.md — colony start (the tutorial's own verified curriculum order),\n  act-keyed checks, event-keyed responses (raid-end carries the INTERIM\n  manual form of cc8988c and retires into the mod when that lands).\n- daily.md — the polling residue: slow event-less drift with no digest field\n  (freezer temp, armament vs roster, bill coverage, apparel margin). The only\n  unconditional recurring cost, hence the ONLY set 4.4's hard cap binds.\n\nThe daily rung survives because the variables it watches move on day scale,\nbecause 4.2's early advances already return about daily (the sweep piggybacks\non a pause the loop makes anyway), and because one verdict per item per day\nis exactly 4.4's retirement evidence. The reshape's concrete payoff: the\nunconditional recurring cost fell from a ~12-item morning read to 4 daily\ndrill-downs; everything else is free-per-turn or priced per firing.\n\nTerminology mapping for 4.2/4.4, so the specs' words still resolve: \"the\nmorning checklist\" = daily.md; 4.4's cap binds daily.md alone (stated in\nchecklists/README.md, one place, N=7 proposed for 4.4 to ratify; current 4).\n\n=====================================================================\nOPEN QUESTION 1 — frontmatter schema (resolved; playbook/README.md is\nnormative)\n=====================================================================\n\nname (slug = filename); trigger (a MOMENT, not a topic); applies-when\n(optional applicability predicate — absent = always; drives the ledger's n/a\nverdict, which is what lets 4.4 tell \"idle\" from \"inapplicable\" — its own\nverification suggested exactly this and it falls out of one field);\nseverity: GoodToKnow | Important | Critical (vanilla OpportunityType per the\namendment; when mining concept defs, severity is read PER CALL SITE, per\ncorrection 3); confidence: verified-in-source | observed-at-bench |\nevan-stated | proposed; source (the citation, non-negotiable). Body fixed:\nWhat / Why / How to apply / Retire when. proposed is the fourth confidence\ntier because the combat-formula handling needed a name: the author's own\ninvention, visible at the claim, awaiting correction.\n\nConfidence ranks trust for MECHANISM only. For POLICY, Evan outranks source,\nwhich has no opinion.\n\n=====================================================================\nOPEN QUESTION 2 — promotion criteria (resolved; postmortem.md is normative)\n=====================================================================\n\nEach rung is a floor, not a queue — findings enter at any rung they qualify\nfor. observation -\u003e prose: survives verification, cited, not derivable from\nalways-loaded files. prose -\u003e checklist: mechanically checkable (names read +\nflag) AND trigger recurs AND missing costs more than watching AND fits a\nmoment class — free-on-digest goes to turn.md, act/event to triggered.md,\nelse daily.md UNDER the cap (entry past cap forces the recorded\nmerge-or-retire). checklist -\u003e template/policy: verifies the same structural\nproperty every time and construction can make it true; graduation DELETES the\nline for template-built instances in the same commit. -\u003e mod: every branch\ncomputable from published observer state (the cc8988c/DESIGN decision,\napplied as a rung); a branch needing a missing read means FILE THE READ, not\nkeep the prose. -\u003e rwtest (needs 5.1): holds in every run; leaves the play\nsurface; 4.4 owns mechanics. Demotion runs the same ladder downhill via 4.4's\npass, weighted by moment-class cost (a daily item's silence accrues pressure;\na trip-wire's silence is success — recorded in checklists/README.md so 4.4\nweighs recurring-cost x silence, not silence alone).\n\n=====================================================================\nOPEN QUESTION 3 — conflicting lessons (resolved; the potato rule)\n=====================================================================\n\nNeither newer-wins nor confidence-wins: a contradiction is a VERIFICATION\nEVENT — decompiled source for mechanism, bench for behaviour. (Recency\nfavoured the wrong side of the potato conflict; the decisions log was right.)\nMechanism belongs to the source; policy belongs to Evan; where his stated\nrule rests on a mechanism the source contradicts, verify and present, never\nsilently override. Resolution lands as ONE winning file in one commit, the\nloser deleted or folded in as a visible correction block whenever the old\nerror taught something (the potato file is the worked example and stays).\nINDEX never lists two live contradicting lessons. applies-when is checked\nfirst — differently-scoped lessons are a map, not a conflict.\n\n=====================================================================\nOPEN QUESTION 4 — template parameter format (resolved; templates/INDEX.md)\n=====================================================================\n\nNo substitution syntax. A template is a concrete worked instance (baseviz IR\nJSON, the ir.py dialect — placeable by 3.3 as-is) plus three parameter\nchannels that already exist at the verb: origin/rotation (place-layout args),\nstuff (tokens are BARE defNames; material binds at placement via --stuff-map,\nwith per-template CONSTRAINTS in the .md — power-room walls must be\nFlammability 0), and variants (a second .ir.json sharing the .md; scaling\nRULES are prose because they are judgement). JSON has no comment channel, so\nthe sibling .md IS the \"templates carry their lessons\" invariant — a patch\ntouches both halves or is not done. Three dialect ambiguities are pinned as\nPROPOSALS for 3.3's own open question (multi-cell anchor = NW cell; rot\nsuffix = facing; layer order = things then conduits), with .md prose\nnormative meanwhile. If freeform resizing is ever wanted, the generator\nbelongs beside the consumer (rwa/3.3, where python lives), consuming the .md\nrules — not an interpreter invented ahead of need.\n\n=====================================================================\nCONTRACT DEFINED FOR 4.2 AND 4.4 — the run ledger\n=====================================================================\n\nRUNS/\u003crun\u003e/checklist.ndjson, one line per evaluation:\n{\"day\":N,\"tick\":T,\"item\":\"\u003cid\u003e\",\"verdict\":\"ok|action|blocked|n/a\",\n\"reading\":\"...\",\"note\":\"...\"}. A silent skip is a MISSING line (4.2's\ninvariant made diffable); \"when did this last fire\" is a grep (4.4's ledger\nmade computable). Trip-wires log firings only; daily/triggered log every\nevaluation. Both specs' verifications asked for one shared artifact; this is\nit, defined in checklists/README.md. Cross-referenced on d32eadd and d2e1229.\n\n=====================================================================\nNEW SOURCE FINDINGS while authoring (all cited in the artifacts)\n=====================================================================\n\n- Alert_LowFood is MUZZLED for the first 150,000 ticks (2.5 days) by\n  GetReport's TicksGame check — a fourth time-scoped alert, and one the\n  recommended GenDate.DaysPassed grep would miss (it keys on ticks). Also its\n  threshold constant (NutritionThresholdPerColonist = 4f) divides by\n  colonists only, while the digest divides by colonists+prisoners — the\n  digest's figure is the conservative one. Folded into turn.md's\n  food-days-floor and the trust table; alert-need-defenses-self-silences.md\n  now tells future mining passes to sweep BOTH idioms.\n- The firefoam popper's TRIGGER is a 3-cell proximity fuse; the 9.9 figure is\n  the foam. The binding placement constraint is the small number. It is\n  one-shot (pops = Destroy), auto-rebuild only arms for a player popper in\n  Home with Firefoam researched, and rebuild is a BLUEPRINT (75 steel + 1\n  component + construction 5) — so protection lapses after every pop, which\n  is the power-incident trigger item.\n- A Zzzt happens ONLY at conduits (GetShortCircuitablePowerConduits\n  enumerates ThingsOfDef(PowerConduit)), centred ON the culprit, radius\n  sqrt(storedWd)*0.05 clamped 1.5-14.9 (+Bomb sub-blast over 3.5); appliances\n  cord to a transmitter within 6 cells (BestTransmitterForConnector,\n  ExpandedBy(6)); batteries over 100 Wd explode in rain. Together these make\n  the power-room template's shape DERIVED rather than folkloric: conduit-free\n  interior, one deliberate conduit under stone, banks sized to their own\n  explosion, roof load-bearing for safety.\n- Apparel mood penalties land at fixed levels — worst worn item under 50%\n  (\"frayed\") and 20% (\"tattered\"), ThoughtWorker_ApparelDamaged — and\n  Alert_TatteredApparel is just that thought made visible. A level read at\n  60% is therefore a leading indicator with NO trend needed; daily.md's\n  apparel-margin runs every 3 days on that basis.\n- A meal rolls poison against the ROOM's FoodPoisonChance stat — a curve over\n  room Cleanliness (0 at \u003e= -2, 2.5 pct at -3.5, 5 pct at -5; flat 2 pct\n  roomless, CompFoodPoisonable.cs:38 + RoomStats.xml). \"Clean kitchen\" is now\n  a number in the freezer-kitchen template.\n- All template footprints and research gates read from the bench's own def\n  XML (Bed 1x2, stoves 3x1, WoodFiredGenerator 2x2, Battery 1x2 at 600 Wd;\n  Cooler needs AirConditioning, generator Electricity, Battery Batteries,\n  popper Firefoam) — 3.3's preflight remains the enforcing check.\n\n=====================================================================\nLESSON EDITS MADE (restructure-freely clause, citations preserved)\n=====================================================================\n\n- who-will-actually-do-it.md promoted observed-at-bench -\u003e\n  verified-in-source per the verification verdict's instruction, carrying\n  WorkGiver_DoBill.ShouldSkip (billGiver != pawn) and\n  WidgetsWork.DrawWorkBoxFor (0/3) into the body.\n- unforbid-before-expecting-pickup.md strengthened with the three FSWA\n  forbidden-check sites and the Alert_NeedWarmClothes IsInAnyStorage pairing\n  (\"loose gear is invisible to every autonomous system\").\n- alert-need-defenses-self-silences.md gains the one-sandbag silencer and\n  the widened time-scoped-alert class (now four instances, two idioms).\n- The corrected potato lesson and the proposed combat formula are untouched\n  and both remain flagged exactly as the handoff required.\n\n=====================================================================\nHONESTLY BLOCKED, SAID IN THE ITEMS THEMSELVES\n=====================================================================\n\n- Every trend item (food slope, wealth-vs-readiness, mood drift) sits in\n  daily.md's \"Blocked on sampling\" section naming 2d9a1da, written as the\n  reads they become — not as single points dressed as slopes.\n- Bill AUTHORING waits on 3.6 and shelter/defence BUILDING on 3.3; the\n  colony-start sequence logs those steps blocked-with-issue-id rather than\n  skipping them. The bill COVERAGE read ships today, as the verification\n  found.\n\nACCEPTANCE STATUS: the dry-run is pinned synthetic and worked INLINE in\npostmortem.md — a six-line journal, the walk, and the three outputs, which\nconverge on artifacts the repo already carries because this loss is the\npre-learned canonical case (that convergence is the demonstration). The\n\"fresh session surfaces all three\" clause is mechanical per the verification's\nfix: SESSION-START.md is an ordered list with named positions, and each\noutput class has a stated surfacing position (lesson -\u003e 1, checklist item -\u003e\n2/3/4 by moment, template patch -\u003e 5). Reviewer can fail it by grep.","files":null}]}